description:
Implement selection that behaves like every desktop program, over rows in display order (as produced above):

```cpp
class Selection
{
public:
    void click(const std::vector<int>& rows, int id, bool ctrl, bool shift);
    bool isSelected(int id) const;
    std::vector<int> selected() const;      // sorted by id
    int anchor() const;                     // -1 when there is none
};
```

| Action | Result |
|---|---|
| Click | Select only `id`; it becomes the anchor |
| Ctrl+click | Toggle `id`, keep the rest; it becomes the anchor |
| Shift+click | Replace the selection with every row from the anchor to `id`, inclusive, in `rows` order |
| Ctrl+Shift+click | Add that range to the current selection |

- With Shift but no anchor (or an anchor not in `rows`), behave like a plain click (or a Ctrl+click, if Ctrl is held too).
- Shift+click does **not** move the anchor, so the user can Shift+click again to change the range end.

